[ci] Gate updates with the benchmark artifact (reviewing)
Integrate benchmark collection and comparison into the existing CI workflow.
Serves: benchmark baselines participate in every future validation run.
Absent: the instrument exists locally but cannot protect updates.
Known by: a CI step that runs the fixed command, compares the committed
baseline, publishes useful artifact data, and remains independent of runner
speed for its pass/fail decision.
Do: extend the current GitHub Actions check only after the artifact and update
rule are stable; preserve the existing model-cache behavior; make asset or
schema failures fatal and keep timeouts as operational safeguards rather than
performance metrics.
Accept: a pull request with changed gated metrics fails with a diff, an
intentional baseline update is reviewable, and no CI decision uses elapsed time,
RSS, CPU utilization, or hardware-specific counters.
-> baseline
-> cost-model
-> grimoire-bridge
> CI comparison must expose the canonical Grimoire description/cut diff, explicit axis/shape diff, CostReport diff, and separately labeled runtime-resource diff. A changed Grimoire source revision, schema/projection version, graph hash, cost-model version, or workload fingerprint is an identity failure until reviewed.
> Implemented in `.github/workflows/ci.yml`: after the existing build/test/lint and cargo-deny checks, CI runs the benchmark package against `/tmp/scry-model-cache` with `--check benchmarks/baseline-v1.json`; the runner fails without overwriting the reference.
> CI first runs `scry-benchmarks --prepare-cache` against `/tmp/scry-model-cache`. This is the explicit network-capable provisioning step; tests and the baseline comparison consume the verified five-file cache and do not rely on test ordering to populate it.
> A clean-cache simulation passed in the CI order: prepare the empty cache, run all-feature workspace tests, then run the baseline `--check`; each returned success and the cache contained the five expected pinned assets.
