> Create a repository benchmark document that defines the command, artifact schema, workload ids, metric bases, memory/FLOP exclusions, model/cache prerequisites, exact-versus-diagnostic fields, and deliberate baseline update process.
> The documentation must state that these are algorithmic work/resource baselines, not claims about machine speed. It must explain why raw RAM/RSS, FLOP/s, elapsed time, and hardware counters are not gates and where diagnostic evidence may be found.
> Keep benchmark interpretation separate from product behavior documentation. Link the benchmark document from the CI or maintainer-facing entry point only after the artifact and command exist; do not make the README promise numbers that planning has not measured.
