[checkpoint] Validate the benchmark system (reviewing)
Review the complete Grimoire-backed static cost and benchmark system before it becomes an update gate.
Serves: future implementation changes are judged against a stable, understood description and cost report.
Absent: a benchmark command can pass while measuring the wrong graph, applying the wrong expressions, or silently dropping a node/shape.
Known by: clean-checkout evidence, a committed canonical Grimoire artifact diff, and validation that contract, Grimoire boundary, operation representation, graph bridge, cost models, workloads, runtime resource seams, runner, baseline, CI, and documentation agree.
Do: verify static addressed structure, operator/group facts, shape/axis extents, named CostReports, runtime-resource basis, identity/version fields, and gate/diagnostic classification together.
Accept: no gated wall-clock/RSS/hardware fields exist; invalid Grimoire, unknown operators, unsupported shapes, malformed artifacts, missing cost assignments, and identity mismatches fail loudly; every gated static cost is recomputable from the canonical description and named cost algebra.
