> The checkpoint now treats the canonical Grimoire description as the primary evidence layer, CostReports as derived projections, and runtime counters as separate observations. A passing scalar cost cannot compensate for a changed or incomplete addressed graph.
> The v1 implementation gate passes locally: format check, strict Clippy, workspace tests, benchmark-feature collector tests, docs, cargo-deny, and the exact baseline `--check` command. The benchmark crate is `publish = false`; only committing the reviewed artifact/CI change and observing the first remote CI run remain outside this execution.
> Acceptance must include a generated description containing at least one opaque operation word such as `Erf` or `Sqrt`, one shape-aware `MatMul` expression, canonical serialization/validation, and a deliberate unknown/unpriced operation failure.
